{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "הביאה לי ציד", :translit "h'vi'ah li tsayid", :gloss "bring me game"} {:he "הביאה למוסר לבך", :translit "h'vi'ah l'musar l'v'kha", :gloss "bring to the discipline of your heart"} {:he "האומרות לאדוניהם הביאה ונשתה", :translit "ha'omrot l'adoneihem h'vi'ah v'nishteh", :gloss "those who say to their masters: bring and we will drink"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["הביאה לי ציד" "הביאה למוסר לבך" "האומרות לאדוניהם הביאה ונשתה"]} {:kind :other, :note "Midrashic reading of למוסר לבך as 'accept my discipline,' reading למוסר as instruction rather than literal 'to the discipline/point of your heart.'"}], :frame {:text "In Genesis 27:5, Rebecca tells Jacob: 'Bring me game and prepare a dish for your father.' The Ba'al HaTurim links the phrase הביאה to Rebecca's instruction to Jacob, reading למוסר לבך as 'accept my discipline (מוסר)' — an echo of Proverbs 1:8, 'My son, hear the discipline (מוסר) of your father, and forsake not the teaching (תורת) of your mother,' understood in Bereshit Rabbah 71:2 as referring to Rebecca. The third Masorah occurrence, האומרות לאדוניהם הביאה ונשתה (Isaiah 22:13), contrasts a call to indulgence with Rebecca's call to obedience.", :sources ["Genesis 27:5" "Proverbs 1:8" "Bereshit Rabbah 71:2" "Isaiah 22:13"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["הביאה לי ציד" "הביאה למוסר לבך" "האומרות לאדוניהם הביאה ונשתה"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "הביאה לי ציד", :refs ["Genesis 27:7"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "הביאה למוסר לבך", :refs ["Proverbs 23:12"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "האומרות לאדוניהם הביאה ונשתה", :refs ["Amos 4:1"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :other, :note "Midrashic reading of למוסר לבך as 'accept my discipline,' reading למוסר as instruction rather than literal 'to the discipline/point of your heart.'", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :discipline "bht-chalkboar